WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.576
- Good Morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.576 --> 00:00:04.409
Today's message is Believe in Joy.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.940
Over to you, John Travolta.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.042
(rooster crows)

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:12.255
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:12.255 --> 00:00:14.496
♫ Espresso keep me going.

00:00:14.496 --> 00:00:18.614
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:18.614 --> 00:00:20.947
- I was always a person
with a lot of confidence

00:00:20.947 --> 00:00:25.812
I'd never took very seriously
anyone making less of me.

00:00:25.812 --> 00:00:28.505
I think you learn by your failures

00:00:28.505 --> 00:00:30.514
and you learn by your mistakes.

00:00:30.514 --> 00:00:32.348
But you don't take them to heart

00:00:32.348 --> 00:00:34.554
because as soon as you do,

00:00:34.554 --> 00:00:36.528
it takes the spirit out of you.

00:00:36.528 --> 00:00:38.943
You die a little bit.

00:00:38.943 --> 00:00:40.860
Look, the world is dark

00:00:42.506 --> 00:00:44.006
as bad as it gets.

00:00:45.096 --> 00:00:46.849
You look in the newspaper, it's bad news.

00:00:46.849 --> 00:00:49.067
You look over your
shoulder, it's bad news.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:50.901
You want me to cry, I'll
cry right now for you.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.898
I can find so much sadness in the world,

00:00:52.898 --> 00:00:56.839
I can find so much tragedy,
I can find so much heartache

00:00:56.839 --> 00:00:59.756
that it will just be massive, okay?

00:01:02.122 --> 00:01:04.063
Now, where's the joy?

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.004
Where's the spirit?

00:01:05.004 --> 00:01:05.837
Where's the fun?

00:01:05.837 --> 00:01:08.289
That's the goal to me.

00:01:08.289 --> 00:01:12.783
I've never understood why so
much is harped on the negative

00:01:12.783 --> 00:01:14.884
because negative is easy.

00:01:14.884 --> 00:01:15.967
Dark is easy.

00:01:16.939 --> 00:01:20.606
Doing it artfully, yes,
we must all do that.

00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:24.276
But, I find it much more interesting

00:01:24.276 --> 00:01:26.401
to find out where the joy is.

00:01:26.401 --> 00:01:27.984
During those times,

00:01:29.141 --> 00:01:33.727
I probably perceived
negative, but I went for life.

00:01:33.727 --> 00:01:35.526
I learned how to become a jet pilot,

00:01:35.526 --> 00:01:36.908
I traveled the world.

00:01:36.908 --> 00:01:39.485
I rubbed elbows with all sorts of people

00:01:39.485 --> 00:01:41.157
and I learned what they were about

00:01:41.157 --> 00:01:42.806
and it was feeding me.

00:01:42.806 --> 00:01:44.025
I had a choice.

00:01:44.025 --> 00:01:47.858
I could've believed that
things were finished,

00:01:49.853 --> 00:01:51.978
things were over.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:55.561
That life is bad, that
life's not worth it.

00:01:57.214 --> 00:01:59.838
Why don't we all die,
or something like that.

00:01:59.838 --> 00:02:02.856
It's not my nature, you see.

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.439
My feeling was that

00:02:07.177 --> 00:02:09.720
you get through that the best you can

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.120
by living life fully and using
the spirit of other people

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.570
to feed you, and you feed them.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.403
You rise above it all that way.

00:02:19.403 --> 00:02:20.262
- I think this is a
really important message

00:02:20.262 --> 00:02:21.690
for entrepreneurs.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.617
I think to be a success
as an entrepreneur,

00:02:23.617 --> 00:02:25.784
you have to be optimistic.

00:02:27.332 --> 00:02:30.606
You have to choose joy over negativity.

00:02:30.606 --> 00:02:33.869
Yes, you can be paranoid and
only the paranoid survive,

00:02:33.869 --> 00:02:36.086
but you have to feel like
it's going to work out.

00:02:36.086 --> 00:02:37.967
Otherwise you get so
lost down in your hole

00:02:37.967 --> 00:02:39.395
that you never come out.

00:02:39.395 --> 00:02:41.926
Entrepreneurs are the
ones who make it out.

00:02:41.926 --> 00:02:44.759
Being a successful entrepreneur is

00:02:45.943 --> 00:02:47.894
one of the hardest things you're
ever going to do in your life.

00:02:47.894 --> 00:02:50.134
The failure rates are crazy.

00:02:50.134 --> 00:02:54.105
85%, 90% of new businesses will fail.

00:02:54.105 --> 00:02:56.021
Yet, here we are trying to do it,

00:02:56.021 --> 00:02:58.319
trying to be the ones who beat the odds

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:00.734
and survive and build something amazing.

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:04.229
Where on paper, the odds are against you.

00:03:04.229 --> 00:03:05.062
You're trying to do something new

00:03:05.062 --> 00:03:06.938
that's never been done before.

00:03:06.938 --> 00:03:07.937
You're not educated for it,

00:03:07.937 --> 00:03:08.993
you don't have the capital for it,

00:03:08.993 --> 00:03:10.781
you don't have the
resources or connections

00:03:10.781 --> 00:03:12.093
or family for it.

00:03:12.093 --> 00:03:15.193
Here you are trying to do it!

00:03:15.193 --> 00:03:16.865
That's what entrepreneurs do.

00:03:16.865 --> 00:03:19.512
You have to choose joy.

00:03:19.512 --> 00:03:24.040
You have to be optimistic
that it's going to work out.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.233
I think the thing that
entrepreneurs are best at

00:03:27.233 --> 00:03:30.576
is recognizing that when
there is some kind of crisis,

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:33.026
when there is something really negative,

00:03:33.026 --> 00:03:37.113
it's thinking about how do
I turn this into a positive?

00:03:37.113 --> 00:03:40.677
It's the example of when
life hands you lemons,

00:03:40.677 --> 00:03:43.568
you make lemonade and you
sell the recipe for it, too.

00:03:43.568 --> 00:03:46.252
That's what an entrepreneur does, right?

00:03:46.252 --> 00:03:47.889
Life is going to hand you tons of lemons.

00:03:47.889 --> 00:03:50.339
Life is going to suck in a lot of ways.

00:03:50.339 --> 00:03:53.195
You're going to get blow
after blow after blow

00:03:53.195 --> 00:03:55.830
in your business life and
in your personal life.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.874
If all you do is stay in your hole,

00:03:57.874 --> 00:03:59.882
you're never going to
create anything amazing.

00:03:59.882 --> 00:04:02.378
You have to look at that crisis,

00:04:02.378 --> 00:04:04.085
that most people would get lost in,

00:04:04.085 --> 00:04:08.252
and say life is terrible
and just complain, right?

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.980
Most people just complain
when something bad

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.582
happens to them, they just complain

00:04:13.582 --> 00:04:15.718
and they blame somebody else.

00:04:15.718 --> 00:04:18.301
The entrepreneur grows from it.

00:04:19.364 --> 00:04:20.873
Builds from it.

00:04:20.873 --> 00:04:22.707
Sees the opportunity in it.

00:04:22.707 --> 00:04:24.797
Gets stronger because of it.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.806
They go off and build something amazing.

00:04:26.806 --> 00:04:29.836
I think this is ingrained
in a lot of entrepreneurs.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.808
But, if it's not you, then
I would encourage you,

00:04:32.808 --> 00:04:34.654
if you're down in the hole right now,

00:04:34.654 --> 00:04:37.963
if you've just been
given successive blows.

00:04:37.963 --> 00:04:40.169
Ask yourself, where's
the opportunity here?

00:04:40.169 --> 00:04:43.327
How can I take what just happened to me,

00:04:43.327 --> 00:04:45.811
all of this stuff that really sucks

00:04:45.811 --> 00:04:48.238
and turn that into something amazing?

00:04:48.238 --> 00:04:50.490
Even just asking that question,

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.487
How do I make this amazing?

00:04:52.487 --> 00:04:54.495
How do I find the opportunity?

00:04:54.495 --> 00:04:57.607
Instead of what you're likely
currently telling yourself,

00:04:57.607 --> 00:05:00.208
"Why does this always happen to me?

00:05:00.208 --> 00:05:02.216
When is it going to get better?"

00:05:02.216 --> 00:05:03.049
Right?

00:05:03.049 --> 00:05:03.882
The complaints.

00:05:03.882 --> 00:05:07.510
Change your questions
to be more optimistic

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:09.389
and you'll get better answers.

00:05:09.389 --> 00:05:10.338
(swoosh)

00:05:10.338 --> 00:05:12.857
So the question today is, I'm curious,

00:05:12.857 --> 00:05:17.757
when was a time in your life
that you needed the most

00:05:17.757 --> 00:05:19.394
to believe in joy?

00:05:19.394 --> 00:05:20.590
Tell me a story.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.330
Share it below. Leave it in the comments.

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:23.807
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:05:23.807 --> 00:05:26.373
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Elita Torres

00:05:26.373 --> 00:05:28.289
from leadgrowdevelop.com,

00:05:28.289 --> 00:05:29.670
Elita, thank you so much for picking up

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.586
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:05:31.586 --> 00:05:34.508
It really, really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:05:34.508 --> 00:05:35.901
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.167
I believe in you.

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.442
I hope you will continue
to believe in yourself

00:05:39.442 --> 00:05:41.335
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:41.335 --> 00:05:42.728
I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:42.728 --> 00:05:45.177
for another shot of Enspresso.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:47.627
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:05:47.627 --> 00:05:51.203
♫ Espresso keep me going.

00:05:51.203 --> 00:05:53.316
Hey guys, there's a special
bonus for this video.

00:05:53.316 --> 00:05:54.744
I'm going to include some extra clips

00:05:54.744 --> 00:05:57.368
on choosing joy, believing in happiness,

00:05:57.368 --> 00:05:58.831
that I hope will also inspire you.

00:05:58.831 --> 00:05:59.664
(swoosh)

00:05:59.664 --> 00:06:01.780
- As you know, I was a
bouncer for many years.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:05.599
I remember coming home one
night after a big fight.

00:06:05.599 --> 00:06:07.306
I run up to the kitchen.

00:06:07.306 --> 00:06:08.455
I get ice.

00:06:08.455 --> 00:06:09.872
My hands swollen.

00:06:11.439 --> 00:06:13.522
Just another day at work.

00:06:15.909 --> 00:06:19.242
I was feeling just bummed about the fact

00:06:20.774 --> 00:06:24.941
that I was still doing this
job after all this time.

00:06:27.972 --> 00:06:30.555
At that one moment, I was like,

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:34.775
why do people have so much anger?

00:06:34.775 --> 00:06:38.942
Why is this my daily life to
suppress everybody's anger

00:06:40.348 --> 00:06:42.879
or check everybody's anger that comes into

00:06:42.879 --> 00:06:45.120
the giant 3,000 person nightclub?

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:45.953
- Mm Hmm.

00:06:45.953 --> 00:06:48.545
- My father, it was so simple,

00:06:48.545 --> 00:06:51.462
but my father said, "You know, Vin,

00:06:52.434 --> 00:06:54.245
I've traveled around the world.

00:06:54.245 --> 00:06:57.229
I've been to India, I've been to Russia,

00:06:57.229 --> 00:07:01.396
I've been to China, I've been
all through South America,

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.936
and I've realized something."

00:07:05.936 --> 00:07:07.186
I said, "What?"

00:07:08.479 --> 00:07:12.396
He said, "People by and
large are good people."

00:07:19.404 --> 00:07:21.154
Sounded pretty simple

00:07:22.051 --> 00:07:24.134
and yet it meant so much.

00:07:25.859 --> 00:07:27.856
If you look at my Facebook page

00:07:27.856 --> 00:07:31.920
or if you look at the way
that all that positive energy,

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:35.182
I don't think there's a page in the world,

00:07:35.182 --> 00:07:39.182
in history, that harbors
as much positive energy

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:45.294
as one would see on this Facebook page.

00:07:45.294 --> 00:07:48.115
- It's what you put out, too, right?

00:07:48.115 --> 00:07:49.782
- I say that because

00:07:52.916 --> 00:07:55.749
if you believe that in your heart,

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.976
and not everybody watching
this can say that,

00:07:59.976 --> 00:08:01.323
or is ready to say that,

00:08:01.323 --> 00:08:04.307
or is comfortable with
themselves enough to say that.

00:08:04.307 --> 00:08:07.662
But, if you really believe in your heart,

00:08:07.662 --> 00:08:11.079
that people by and large are good people,

00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:16.242
it affects the way that
you address the world.

00:08:16.242 --> 00:08:18.992
As you see, post in and post out,

00:08:21.106 --> 00:08:24.023
I address a world that, in my soul,

00:08:25.286 --> 00:08:28.203
I feel is comprised of good people.

00:08:29.431 --> 00:08:30.322
(swoosh)

00:08:30.322 --> 00:08:33.322
- My message was just find
peace within yourself.

00:08:33.322 --> 00:08:35.951
Once you find peace within yourself,

00:08:35.951 --> 00:08:38.029
the energy that you get
usually is reflected.

00:08:38.029 --> 00:08:40.769
People get that energy off of you.

00:08:40.769 --> 00:08:42.162
That's what I've been able to find

00:08:42.162 --> 00:08:45.309
from being, you know, on
the negative energy side

00:08:45.309 --> 00:08:46.992
as a young artist

00:08:46.992 --> 00:08:51.159
to a grown man that projects
positive and peaceful music.

00:08:52.205 --> 00:08:54.004
But it still has the
energy of the young spirit.

00:08:54.004 --> 00:08:55.839
It's all within the same realm,

00:08:55.839 --> 00:08:56.895
but it's just finding yourself

00:08:56.895 --> 00:08:59.357
and being able to be within
yourself and have peace.

00:08:59.357 --> 00:09:01.400
That way you can project peace.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.909
Especially on the Internet,

00:09:02.909 --> 00:09:06.427
you can get pulled into a
whole lot of negative energy.

00:09:06.427 --> 00:09:09.086
I've done things where
I've put pictures up,

00:09:09.086 --> 00:09:11.501
and read comments, and then
I'll say something back

00:09:11.501 --> 00:09:13.509
and I end up arguing with
somebody on the Internet

00:09:13.509 --> 00:09:15.146
that I don't even know.

00:09:15.146 --> 00:09:17.120
I'm like, you've done pulled
me all the way out of my skin.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.800
It's just the point of
knowing your limitations

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.205
as far as where you'll go

00:09:22.205 --> 00:09:25.514
and let people take you out
of your frame of who you are.

00:09:25.514 --> 00:09:28.869
I'll never allow nobody to
take me out of the mind state

00:09:28.869 --> 00:09:31.272
that I'm supposed to be
in, know what I'm sayin'?

00:09:31.272 --> 00:09:32.584
Never let 'em see me sweat.

00:09:32.584 --> 00:09:36.137
Never let 'em see me deal with adversity

00:09:36.137 --> 00:09:36.970
as if I can't deal with it.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:37.910
(swoosh)

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.690
- If you're going to be
successful in creating

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:41.164
the life of your dreams,

00:09:41.164 --> 00:09:43.080
you have to believe that you

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.262
are capable of making it happen.

00:09:45.262 --> 00:09:47.352
You have to believe that
you have the right stuff

00:09:47.352 --> 00:09:49.477
and that you're able to pull it off.

00:09:49.477 --> 00:09:52.321
Whether you call it self
esteem, self confidence,

00:09:52.321 --> 00:09:53.738
or self assurance,

00:09:53.738 --> 00:09:57.012
it's a deep seeded belief
that you have what it takes.

00:09:57.012 --> 00:09:59.055
The abilities, the inner resources,

00:09:59.055 --> 00:10:03.200
the talents and the skills to
create your desired results.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:06.068
Believing in yourself
is simply an attitude.

00:10:06.068 --> 00:10:08.564
Believing in yourself is a choice.

00:10:08.564 --> 00:10:10.967
You have to choose to
believe that you can do

00:10:10.967 --> 00:10:13.045
anything you set your mind to.

00:10:13.045 --> 00:10:14.357
Anything at all.

00:10:14.357 --> 00:10:16.644
Because, in fact, you can.

00:10:16.644 --> 00:10:17.619
It might help you to know

00:10:17.619 --> 00:10:20.325
that the latest brain
research now indicates

00:10:20.325 --> 00:10:22.171
with enough positive self talk

00:10:22.171 --> 00:10:23.889
and positive visualization,

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:26.664
combined with proper training,
coaching, and practice,

00:10:26.664 --> 00:10:29.810
anyone can learn to do almost anything.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:32.515
I've interviewed thousands
of successful people.

00:10:32.515 --> 00:10:34.686
Almost every one of them has told me,

00:10:34.686 --> 00:10:36.079
"I was not the most gifted or

00:10:36.079 --> 00:10:38.134
the most talented person in my field,

00:10:38.134 --> 00:10:41.826
but I chose to believe
that anything was possible.

00:10:41.826 --> 00:10:44.125
Because of that, I studied, I practiced,

00:10:44.125 --> 00:10:45.797
and I worked harder than the others,

00:10:45.797 --> 00:10:47.887
and that's how I got to where I am."

00:10:47.887 --> 00:10:52.763
If Reuben Gonzalez, a 20
year old living in hot Texas,

00:10:52.763 --> 00:10:55.294
can take up the luge,
which is a winter sport,

00:10:55.294 --> 00:10:57.221
and become an Olympic athlete,

00:10:57.221 --> 00:11:00.008
if Bill Gates, who was a college dropout,

00:11:00.008 --> 00:11:02.457
can become a multi billionaire,

00:11:02.457 --> 00:11:05.278
and Stephen J. Cannell,
who was a dyslexic student,

00:11:05.278 --> 00:11:07.566
who failed three grades in school,

00:11:07.566 --> 00:11:10.538
can become a best selling author
and a television producer,

00:11:10.538 --> 00:11:12.964
then you, too, can accomplish anything

00:11:12.964 --> 00:11:15.739
if you'll simply believe it's possible.

00:11:15.739 --> 00:11:17.260
Make the decision right now

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:20.279
to believe that you create
all of your experiences.

00:11:20.279 --> 00:11:21.881
Because you do.

00:11:21.881 --> 00:11:23.843
Let's start creating the ones you want

00:11:23.843 --> 00:11:25.526
by believing you can.

00:11:25.526 --> 00:11:26.827
Sounds a little strange,

00:11:26.827 --> 00:11:29.149
but accepting this level of responsibility

00:11:29.149 --> 00:11:32.144
is uniquely and inevitably empowering.

00:11:32.144 --> 00:11:35.685
It means you can do, change,
and become anything at all.

00:11:35.685 --> 00:11:36.518
(swoosh)

00:11:36.518 --> 00:11:38.193
- If you have this crazy idea,

00:11:38.193 --> 00:11:42.245
you must believe in it
even if no one else does.

00:11:42.245 --> 00:11:45.600
When I had the idea to go to
every country in the world,

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.084
it felt like this crazy idea.

00:11:48.084 --> 00:11:50.453
It was like, this just sounds
totally ridiculous and absurd,

00:11:50.453 --> 00:11:52.682
but I couldn't stop thinking about it.

00:11:52.682 --> 00:11:55.654
I realized that if I didn't pursue it,

00:11:55.654 --> 00:11:57.988
I would always regret it.

00:11:57.988 --> 00:12:02.597
That knowledge, that fear of
regret drove me to say yes.

00:12:02.597 --> 00:12:03.886
I talked to lots of other people who used

00:12:03.886 --> 00:12:05.720
very similar language.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:07.601
There's a guy from Portland, Maine,

00:12:07.601 --> 00:12:10.701
whose crazy idea was
to walk across America.

00:12:10.701 --> 00:12:12.651
He wasn't even sure how that worked,

00:12:12.651 --> 00:12:15.407
how long does it take, has
anyone done this before.

00:12:15.407 --> 00:12:17.486
It was this crazy idea that
wouldn't leave him alone.

00:12:17.486 --> 00:12:20.342
So, one morning he left his home in Maine

00:12:20.342 --> 00:12:23.453
and he started walking, and
seven and a half months later,

00:12:23.453 --> 00:12:25.914
he arrived in San Francisco.

00:12:25.914 --> 00:12:27.691
I talked to him throughout
the whole journey.

00:12:27.691 --> 00:12:29.397
I talked to him in the beginning,
the middle and the end.

00:12:29.397 --> 00:12:32.045
I asked him, "What were
the challenges like?

00:12:32.045 --> 00:12:33.147
How did it go?"

00:12:33.147 --> 00:12:34.784
He said something that stayed with me

00:12:34.784 --> 00:12:36.549
for the rest of my journey.

00:12:36.549 --> 00:12:41.414
He said, "You know there were
lots of external challenges.

00:12:41.414 --> 00:12:43.654
It was hard on the body to
get used to walking that much.

00:12:43.654 --> 00:12:45.175
Lots of things went wrong."

00:12:45.175 --> 00:12:47.463
There were some emotional
challenges as well.

00:12:47.463 --> 00:12:48.693
He had just had a break up and

00:12:48.693 --> 00:12:50.771
he was processing all of this.

00:12:50.771 --> 00:12:53.268
He said, "What I realized
about two weeks in,

00:12:53.268 --> 00:12:55.799
once I stopped complaining and grumbling

00:12:55.799 --> 00:12:57.470
about the whole thing,

00:12:57.470 --> 00:13:01.557
I realized that my task was pretty simple.

00:13:01.557 --> 00:13:03.728
All I had to do was walk, essentially.

00:13:03.728 --> 00:13:06.456
If I did nothing else, if
I got up every morning,

00:13:06.456 --> 00:13:08.500
and I made a little bit of progress,

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:10.706
then eventually I would reach the goal.

00:13:10.706 --> 00:13:12.343
Eventually I would arrive in San Francisco

00:13:12.343 --> 00:13:15.849
and achieve that goal and
reach that destination."

00:13:15.849 --> 00:13:17.498
It sounded really simple,

00:13:17.498 --> 00:13:21.561
but it stayed with me for the
final two years of my quest.

00:13:21.561 --> 00:13:23.140
That's how I felt it was for me, too.

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:25.764
All I had to do was get to 193 countries.

00:13:25.764 --> 00:13:27.772
I had my list of countries.

00:13:27.772 --> 00:13:29.038
I was making progress.

00:13:29.038 --> 00:13:30.628
If I got stuck somewhere,

00:13:30.628 --> 00:13:32.254
eventually I would have to
overcome that challenge,

00:13:32.254 --> 00:13:34.506
but I could go and do some others first.

00:13:34.506 --> 00:13:37.780
I like the logical,
analytical progress of it.

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:39.173
It's something that related to me.

00:13:39.173 --> 00:13:40.067
Just keep going.

00:13:40.067 --> 00:13:42.353
You have to believe in your
dream even if no one else does.

